# Third-Party Material Notice

## Toolchain build

The toolchain cross-builds an LLVM/Clang driver to WebAssembly and runs it on
Wasmer. It uses these upstream projects:

- [wasmerio/wasmer](https://github.com/wasmerio/wasmer), MIT licensed (Copyright (c) 2019-present Wasmer, Inc.), documents the WASIX compile, shared-memory, thread, TLS, and signal ABI and provides the runtime that executes the driver.
- [wasix-org/wasix-libc](https://github.com/wasix-org/wasix-libc) supplies the WASIX sysroot under MIT, Apache-2.0, and Apache-2.0-LLVM.
- [WebAssembly/wasi-sdk](https://github.com/WebAssembly/wasi-sdk) 25.0 supplies the wasm cross-compiler under Apache-2.0 WITH LLVM-exception.
- [llvm/llvm-project](https://github.com/llvm/llvm-project) `llvmorg-19.1.6` supplies LLVM and Clang under Apache-2.0 WITH LLVM-exception.

`toolchain/src/scripts/wasix_toolchain.cmake` is this repository's own implementation of the publicly documented WASIX flag set. `toolchain/src/patches/wasix-compat.patch` modifies files in the pinned LLVM source to support this cross-build; those modified LLVM files remain under LLVM's Apache-2.0 WITH LLVM-exception license.

## Simulator

`simulator` builds against two upstream simulators, wired in through `replace` directives in `go.mod` and pinned in `pins.env`:

- [sarchlab/akita](https://github.com/sarchlab/akita) v5, MIT licensed (Copyright (c) 2017 Yifan Sun), provides the discrete-event simulation framework.
- [sarchlab/mgpusim](https://github.com/sarchlab/mgpusim) v5, MIT licensed (Copyright (c) 2017 Project Akita Authors), provides the GPU timing model, instruction decoder, and wave execution.

`simulator/third_party/akita_patches/` records this repository's local changes to akita, which add `js/wasm` build support. Those modified akita files remain under akita's MIT license.

`simulator/third_party/mgpusim_patches/` records this repository's local changes to mgpusim, which add a GCN3 LDS bank-conflict analyzer. Those modified and added mgpusim files remain under mgpusim's MIT license.

## Go modules

- [open-telemetry/opentelemetry-proto-go](https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-proto-go) via `go.opentelemetry.io/proto/otlp`, Apache-2.0, supplies the OTLP metrics and traces protobuf definitions.
- [protocolbuffers/protobuf-go](https://github.com/protocolbuffers/protobuf-go) via `google.golang.org/protobuf`, BSD-3-Clause (Copyright (c) 2018 The Go Authors), is its runtime.

The remaining indirect Go dependencies are pulled in by akita and mgpusim and retain their upstream licenses.

